{
  "header": [
    "Benny Boys Pizza",
    "Menu & Pizza Making Guideline",
    "100 Coleman Rd, Wantirna South, VIC 3152 | (03) 9801 2861",
    "Menu and prices are transcribed from File 1. Preparation instructions are included where a matching pizza recipe appears in File 2. Original source wording is retained where practical."
  ],
  "standardSteps": [
    "Before service: Take dough balls out to come to room temperature and rest so they stretch without tearing. Portion sauce, cheese and toppings into labelled containers with a scoop for each. Toppings must be cooked, drained and cold from the fridge. Preheat the oven fully.",
    "1. Stretch the dough: Use one dough ball per pizza: 220g Small, 330g Large, 480g Family. Stretch by hand to the edge of the pan or screen. Keep the edge slightly thicker. No holes.",
    "2. Sauce: Spiral the sauce from the centre outward with the ladle (60 / 90 / 140g), leaving a 1cm rim of bare dough.",
    "3. Cheese: Spread mozzarella evenly right to the sauce edge. Weigh it - cheese is your biggest cost. Double-cheese pizzas (Margherita, Pepperoni) use the higher weight.",
    "4. Toppings: Meats first, then vegetables, then feta or egg last. One even layer, no piles in the centre. Drain wet items (pineapple, capsicum, olives, mussels, jalapenos) so the centre stays crisp. Follow the build order on each pizza card.",
    "5. Bake: Bake until the crust is golden, cheese is melted and lightly spotted, and the base is firm when lifted. Time and temperature depend on your oven - set them once, write them on the oven and keep them the same every time.",
    "6. Finish: Add drizzles and garnishes shown under AFTER THE OVEN. Cut, then box (9\" / 12\" / 15\" box). Check the order slip against the box before closing the lid.",
    "Quality check: Right size, right toppings, even cover, no bare patches, no burnt edge, cheese melted, cut all the way through. Remake anything that fails, and log remakes to track waste.",
    "Hygiene and allergens: Wash hands and change gloves after handling raw egg or raw meat. Use clean tools for gluten-free bases. Tell customers about allergens on request (menu allergen advisory).",
    "Rules that change the toppings: Only 1-2 meats on the pizza = meat +25%. Loaded pizzas (6+ toppings) = toppings -20%. Gluten-free base: same build, note it on the docket."
  ],
